  "decision_date": "07/10/2005",
  "description": "Conversion of houses into a single dwelling incorporating a first floor rear extension and roof extension to No. 17 and a two-storey rear infill extension to both houses.",
  "site_name": "17 &19",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "09/10/2005",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "TW3 2NA",
  "street_name": "Park Avenue",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "lapsed_date": "06/10/2010",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - Subject to appropriate safeguarding conditions, the proposed conversion of two houses into one single-family house, and the proposed extensions and alterations, because of their compatible design and appearance, and relative position to adjoining properties, would be compatible with the character and appearance of the property and the street scene, and would not harm neighbours' living conditions. The proposal would therefore accord with adopted Unitary Development Plan policies ENV-B.1.1 (New Development), H.6.4 (Extensions and Alterations) and the objectives of the Council's Residential Extension Guidelines.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 4 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the extensions are used.",
    "Condition : 5 - No additional flank windows or other glazed openings shall be formed in the any wall or roof slope the extensions hereby approved without the prior written consent of the Local Planning Authority."
  ],
